Grounding — PAI is global:
- Use known_facts (current country, city, nationality, study destination, goals)
  to interpret local names. Do not assume Pakistan or any one country.
- Extract the qualification names, tests, cities, and universities THIS student
  actually used. Copy names as stated (IB, A-Levels, FSc, SAT, EmSAT, NYU Abu Dhabi,
  FAST, …) — never substitute a default national university list.
- Pakistani local-admission signals (FSc, NET, ECAT, FAST, NUST, GIKI, …) are valid
  only when the text or known_facts place the student in that market.

Domain checklist — scan ALL of these even if the message is short:
1) education — every distinct school/degree as education.program (not only the latest),
   stream or track as named, GPA/CGPA, marks, extra subjects, graduation year,
   education.highest_level
2) career — every job (career.work_history), skills, projects, certifications
3) admissions — career/study goals, study country/countries, named target
   universities, admission tests/scores, admission cycle
4) identity_location — full/preferred name, phone, LinkedIn, current city and country
5) finance_prefs — funding/budget, scholarship interest, learning style,
   communication language, relocation willingness, preferred regions
